course: dictionary
lesson: 8275
title: One word, many meanings: rim
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A rim is the edge or border around the top of something round. The same word can mean different things, so the context tells you which one. «The speed a bike loses when it brakes turns into heat in the pads and rim» means the outer edge of a bike wheel, where the tyre fits.
explain: «Pitcher plants have jug-shaped leaves with slippery rims» means the edges around the top of the leaf-jug. Check by swapping in your meaning: "the slippery edge of the jug" still makes sense, so you have found the right one.
explain: Rim can also be a verb. «Eyes rimmed with red» means the eyes have a red edge around them, as if a line had been drawn round them. The word eyes is the clue, because you can only put an edge around something.
fact: A rim is the edge or border around the top of something round, like a cup, bowl or glass.
fact: The rim of a bike wheel is the outer edge that the tyre fits on.
fact: The rim of glasses is the frame that goes around the lenses.
fact: «Rim» can also be a verb, meaning to form an edge around something.
fact: In maths, a rim is the circle at the edge of a cylinder or circle shape.
exercise: «Use only microwave-safe dishes: metal, foil and gold rims make sparks.» What is a rim here? | *The edge around the top or outside of a dish | A gold coin | A microwave door | A kind of spark
exercise: «You do not hang on the basketball rim, because the hoop or you can fall.» What is the rim? | *The metal ring of the hoop | The ball itself | The floor of the court | The net under the hoop
exercise: Which phrase names the countries around the Pacific Ocean? | Ocean Floor | Ring of Water | *Pacific Rim | Pacific Wave
test: «The crater rim was steep and jagged.» What does rim mean here? | *The edge around the top of a crater | A kind of rock | The bottom of a hole | The inside wall of the crater
test: «The bike wheel rim was bent after the crash.» What was bent? | *The outer edge of the wheel | The brake pads | The air inside the tyre | The handlebars
exam: «Her eyes were rimmed with red after the sad film.» What does rimmed mean here? | Were covered in paint | *Had a red edge around them | Were closed tightly | Were shining brightly
